  "problem": "Consider the following scenarios:\n\n- A card is drawn from a standard $52$-card deck and put back into the deck. Then, a second card is drawn. Let ${A}_{1}$ be the event \"The first card is an Ace,\" and let ${A}_{2}$ be the event \"the second card is an Ace.\"\n\n- A card is drawn from a standard $52$-card deck and set aside. Then, a second card is drawn. Let ${H}_{1}$ be the event \"the first card is a heart,\" and ${H}_{2}$ be the event \"the second card is a heart.\"\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${A}_{1}$ and ${A}_{2}$ are independent\n\nII. ${A}_{1}$ and ${A}_{2}$ are dependent\n\nIII. ${H}_{1}$ and ${H}_{2}$ are independent",
